(428925, 38424, 9504, '<td valign="top">This is a special image. It really says, "At Rest" to me. I love the black and white, the reflection, the subject.  I wish you didn''t crop off the bottom of the reflection but otherwise it is perfect! 10</td>', 'This is a special image. It really says, "At Rest" to me. I love the black and white, the reflection, the subject.  I wish you didn''t crop off the bottom of the reflection but otherwise it is perfect! 10', '2003-09-24 16:18:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(428926, 38393, 9504, '<td valign="top">This photo says "At Rest" to me.  There is peace to it.  The photo is crisp, yet there is a softness to the photo.  You''ve got my top vote.  10</td>', 'This photo says "At Rest" to me.  There is peace to it.  The photo is crisp, yet there is a softness to the photo.  You''ve got my top vote.  10', '2003-09-24 16:19:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(428928, 38365, 11114, '<td valign="top">sexy - provocative - nice lighting - not restful tho</td>', 'sexy - provocative - nice lighting - not restful tho', '2003-09-24 16:20:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(428929, 39247, 3867, '<td valign="top">I love dolphins and this is a beautiful shot of some but they don''t look at rest.  I''m sure your going to get a ton of comments from other voters telling you they''re not at rest (the voters on this site love to point out the obvious) so I won''t dwell on that.  The dolphin below the top one is a bit blurred.  I can''t tell if its from movement or depth of field.  I''m guessing to freeze the top dolphin you used a pretty fast shutter speed so its probably a DOF problem.  Setting your camera''s ASA setting (if it has one) to a higher setting might have solved this.  That''s a knit pic though.  I realize how difficult it is to shoot moving animals so that said, you did a great job.</td>', 'I love dolphins and this is a beautiful shot of some but they don''t look at rest.  I''m sure your going to get a ton of comments from other voters telling you they''re not at rest (the voters on this site love to point out the obvious) so I won''t dwell on that.  The dolphin below the top one is a bit blurred.  I can''t tell if its from movement or depth of field.  I''m guessing to freeze the top dolphin you used a pretty fast shutter speed so its probably a DOF problem.  Setting your camera''s ASA setting (if it has one) to a higher setting might have solved this.  That''s a knit pic though.  I realize how difficult it is to shoot moving animals so that said, you did a great job.', '2003-09-24 16:20:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(428931, 38424, 11114, '<td valign="top">would like to see this in colour - it''s very nice</td>', 'would like to see this in colour - it''s very nice', '2003-09-24 16:20:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(428932, 38729, 9504, '<td valign="top">I love this photo.  Great mood captured!  9<br/></td>', 'I love this photo.  Great mood captured!  9', '2003-09-24 16:21:41.000000', NULL, 1),
