(436016, 39411, 11895, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who commented on my first challenge entry.  I wish I had done a better job on what I felt was a very appropriate subject.</td>', 'Thanks to all who commented on my first challenge entry.  I wish I had done a better job on what I felt was a very appropriate subject.', '2003-10-01 01:46:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(436050, 39296, 5728, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all your comments for this photo. It really didn''t turn out the way I wanted though and I am surprised that it scored so well. I took this on holiday in Russia and processed it on my laptop which I had with me. When I saw it on my desktop once the voting had started it looked completely different. The sepia toning is too extreme, the contrast is too low and it is lighter than I wanted. I never realised there is so much difference between laptop and computer screens.<br/> <br/>A few of you mentioned the angle of the bench, well it was sloped like that. Actually so was the fence and the house. This village is from 1703 and everything is on a lean in one or the other direction.<br/> <br/>And yes she let me take her photo. Way out in the Urals where I went, people hardly ever see anyone else outside of their villages and were so happy to see us and have their photos taken.</td>', 'Thanks for all your comments for this photo. It really didn''t turn out the way I wanted though and I am surprised that it scored so well. I took this on holiday in Russia and processed it on my laptop which I had with me. When I saw it on my desktop once the voting had started it looked completely different. The sepia toning is too extreme, the contrast is too low and it is lighter than I wanted. I never realised there is so much difference between laptop and computer screens. A few of you mentioned the angle of the bench, well it was sloped like that. Actually so was the fence and the house. This village is from 1703 and everything is on a lean in one or the other direction. And yes she let me take her photo. Way out in the Urals where I went, people hardly ever see anyone else outside of their villages and were so happy to see us and have their photos taken.', '2003-10-01 02:09:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(436069, 39404, 5728, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your first ribbon Richard. And well deserved too.</td>', 'Congratulations on your first ribbon Richard. And well deserved too.', '2003-10-01 02:21:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(436073, 38393, 9073, '<td valign="top">What a lovely photograph. <br/> <br/>What''s the expression, 3 heads are better than one? I love the way the baby''s head is juxtaposed with the soft toys, showing a real feeling of softness for the baby. <br/> <br/>Well done.</td>', 'What a lovely photograph.  What''s the expression, 3 heads are better than one? I love the way the baby''s head is juxtaposed with the soft toys, showing a real feeling of softness for the baby.  Well done.', '2003-10-01 02:23:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(436075, 39369, 5728, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Linda on your first ribbon. This photo is beautiful, I love the warm tones.</td>', 'Congratulations Linda on your first ribbon. This photo is beautiful, I love the warm tones.', '2003-10-01 02:24:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(436085, 39070, 9073, '<td valign="top">Great and funny shot. Well done, Tarique. <br/> <br/>The use of light is very good. I can''t agree at all with the commentator below who complained about the top shadow; the shadow curve is one of the strongest elements here. <br/> <br/>There are some problems with the sizing: artifacts and impure lines in the shadows under the chair and sitting thing. The spots on the egg don''t help, neither does the lack of texture on front of the egg. When you resize it and put it on your portfolio, I''m sure the results will be great.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Great and funny shot. Well done, Tarique.  The use of light is very good. I can''t agree at all with the commentator below who complained about the top shadow; the shadow curve is one of the strongest elements here.  There are some problems with the sizing: artifacts and impure lines in the shadows under the chair and sitting thing. The spots on the egg don''t help, neither does the lack of texture on front of the egg. When you resize it and put it on your portfolio, I''m sure the results will be great. ', '2003-10-01 02:29:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(436087, 39059, 9040, '<td valign="top">Thanks the comments guys:) I took this in a cave:) It''s height was 10 cm only :) and I didn''t wake up it:) The lighning was the flash of A200 ;)</td>', 'Thanks the comments guys:) I took this in a cave:) It''s height was 10 cm only :) and I didn''t wake up it:) The lighning was the flash of A200 ;)', '2003-10-01 02:29:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(436095, 38801, 5728, '<td valign="top">Close Rob, close! I had a feeling this was another Brighton Pier shot, Good one Rob. I like the way you got those yachts in between the deckchairs there.<br/> <br/>By the way, don''t you guys have anything else to take photos of in Brighton except your pier?</td>', 'Close Rob, close! I had a feeling this was another Brighton Pier shot, Good one Rob. I like the way you got those yachts in between the deckchairs there. By the way, don''t you guys have anything else to take photos of in Brighton except your pier?', '2003-10-01 02:31:32.000000', NULL, 0),
