(436198, 38729, 10752, '<td valign="top">Thank you all guys!!!<br/> <br/>You really help me enough to try harder and spot to what I have to do. This 50 days old kitten was photographed under an arbor, so the spots are sun beams that comes to my frame. "Ivan" (the name of the cat) was resting on the thighes of my wife surrended to her caresses. I made him a "star" so I ''m gonna have news from Ivan by phone every week. He lives among 10 cats, 3 dogs and 7 horses in an equestrian club at the North part of Euboea Island in Greece. I hope he''s gonna make it! I''ll turn back with some future photos of him...</td>', 'Thank you all guys!!! You really help me enough to try harder and spot to what I have to do. This 50 days old kitten was photographed under an arbor, so the spots are sun beams that comes to my frame. "Ivan" (the name of the cat) was resting on the thighes of my wife surrended to her caresses. I made him a "star" so I ''m gonna have news from Ivan by phone every week. He lives among 10 cats, 3 dogs and 7 horses in an equestrian club at the North part of Euboea Island in Greece. I hope he''s gonna make it! I''ll turn back with some future photos of him...', '2003-10-01 06:02:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(436231, 39404, 7261, '<td valign="top">This is the best winner I have seen since I joined DPC.</td>', 'This is the best winner I have seen since I joined DPC.', '2003-10-01 07:23:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(436259, 39103, 10437, '<td valign="top">Thank you so much for the nice comments left on my picture and specially to the people who gave me high votes.<br/> <br/>My submission is in no way a ribbon winner, but I will never understand what people mean when they give it a 1 or even a 2<br/> <br/>Mysteries I will never solve!</td>', 'Thank you so much for the nice comments left on my picture and specially to the people who gave me high votes. My submission is in no way a ribbon winner, but I will never understand what people mean when they give it a 1 or even a 2 Mysteries I will never solve!', '2003-10-01 07:44:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(436265, 38852, 9977, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by WesF:</b></div><hr/><i>A wonderfully composed protrait!  The only thing I see is the detail in her blouse is out of focus.  This could be just a depth of field issue.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>I think that is not really an issue, it''s certainly due to the canon teleobjectif, at F4.0 and at long it is a really small range for DOF.<br/> <br/>Thank you for your comment<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-01 08:15:35.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by WesF:A wonderfully composed protrait!  The only thing I see is the detail in her blouse is out of focus.  This could be just a depth of field issue. I think that is not really an issue, it''s certainly due to the canon teleobjectif, at F4.0 and at long it is a really small range for DOF. Thank you for your comment', '2003-10-01 07:51:04.000000', '2003-10-01 09:15:35.000000', 0),
(436288, 39161, 472, '<td valign="top">hmm - prolly should have just called it ''at rest'' or ''night time'' :P<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-01 07:47:02.</i></td>', 'hmm - prolly should have just called it ''at rest'' or ''night time'' :P', '2003-10-01 08:46:41.000000', '2003-10-01 08:47:02.000000', 0),
(436292, 38852, 9977, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by banmorn:</b></div><hr/><i>nice portraiture. no implication of being at rest as the model, though cute, is posing for the camera.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Valentine is a very kind but unruly niece, she was playing and running a lot before the shoot, she really stopped and stayed at rest against the tree for 1 or 2 seconds, I took around 20 pictures before this one, and you would see it''s completely different. <br/>She was not posing, but resting tired of playing a lot... I can''t catch this expression on her face anymore, unless I am lucky ...<br/> <br/>Anyway the main goal was to give a calm mood around the shoot.<br/>Thank you for your comment.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by banmorn:nice portraiture. no implication of being at rest as the model, though cute, is posing for the camera.  Valentine is a very kind but unruly niece, she was playing and running a lot before the shoot, she really stopped and stayed at rest against the tree for 1 or 2 seconds, I took around 20 pictures before this one, and you would see it''s completely different. She was not posing, but resting tired of playing a lot... I can''t catch this expression on her face anymore, unless I am lucky ... Anyway the main goal was to give a calm mood around the shoot.Thank you for your comment.', '2003-10-01 08:47:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(436294, 39367, 472, '<td valign="top">no sense of humor on this site .. :/</td>', 'no sense of humor on this site .. :/', '2003-10-01 08:48:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(436296, 38852, 9977, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by uabresch:</b></div><hr/><i>Beautiful smile and eyes, good picture.  Did you try cropping a bit more off the top of the picture, maybe right below the little yellow mark at the top right?  I wonder if the picture might be a bit more effective that way.  Something to try.  It''s a beautiful picture as it is though.  ~8</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you very much for your comments, I tried and you''re right, it''s better. Do you know how to remove the hair from her mouth (Photoshop or photoshop elements).<br/> <br/>Thank you for sharing your experience and knowledge with us.<br/>Rui Felipe<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-01 08:14:33.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by uabresch:Beautiful smile and eyes, good picture.  Did you try cropping a bit more off the top of the picture, maybe right below the little yellow mark at the top right?  I wonder if the picture might be a bit more effective that way.  Something to try.  It''s a beautiful picture as it is though.  ~8  Thank you very much for your comments, I tried and you''re right, it''s better. Do you know how to remove the hair from her mouth (Photoshop or photoshop elements). Thank you for sharing your experience and knowledge with us.Rui Felipe', '2003-10-01 08:49:54.000000', '2003-10-01 09:14:33.000000', 0),
