(436304, 38852, 9977, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Zeissman:</b></div><hr/><i>too bad you couldn''t have removed that hair from her mouth, otherwise great</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes you are right, I don''t know how to do it (after shot) I had only 1 or 2 seconds to take the shot, and it was difficult to manage hair removing. Although I don''t seen it at the shooting time (due to fact I had to shoot very quickly to catch this expression, If she was posing I would had the time to remove it). I would like to know how to remove it in the final picture, does someone can help me (Photosho or Photoshop Elements).<br/>Thanks a lot.<br/>Rui Felipe<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-01 08:13:24.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Zeissman:too bad you couldn''t have removed that hair from her mouth, otherwise great Yes you are right, I don''t know how to do it (after shot) I had only 1 or 2 seconds to take the shot, and it was difficult to manage hair removing. Although I don''t seen it at the shooting time (due to fact I had to shoot very quickly to catch this expression, If she was posing I would had the time to remove it). I would like to know how to remove it in the final picture, does someone can help me (Photosho or Photoshop Elements).Thanks a lot.Rui Felipe', '2003-10-01 08:53:23.000000', '2003-10-01 09:13:24.000000', 0),
