(436316, 38852, 9977, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by clues56:</b></div><hr/><i>A beautiful little girl!!  And the lighting of her soft skin is perfect.  Having her rest against the tree adds a little dreaminess to it.   One of the bes children photographs I''ve seen</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It''s true she was not lying, sitting, sleeping ... at rest. But she really was at rest after playing and running everywhere, it was the first time I seen this expression on her face ... and it lasted only 1 second ...<br/> <br/>Thank you very much all for your kind comments, I am very happy.</td>', 'Originally posted by clues56:A beautiful little girl!!  And the lighting of her soft skin is perfect.  Having her rest against the tree adds a little dreaminess to it.   One of the bes children photographs I''ve seen  It''s true she was not lying, sitting, sleeping ... at rest. But she really was at rest after playing and running everywhere, it was the first time I seen this expression on her face ... and it lasted only 1 second ... Thank you very much all for your kind comments, I am very happy.', '2003-10-01 08:58:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(436330, 38852, 9977, '<td valign="top">Here is a Valentine''s picture 1 minute before the shot... She is always playing an running everywhere, she never stops!<br/>She is always laughing a lot, but not as in picture above, it was the first time I could catch a resting, smooth and calm smile like this one, I took the picture when she turned her face to me, I had about one second to shoot her, the second after she was running and playing again.<br/> <br/>//www.betterphoto.com/uploads/processed/0014/0309211307291pc01b.jpg<br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.betterphoto.com/uploads/processed/0014/0309211307291pc01b.jpg'', strrpos(''//www.betterphoto.com/uploads/processed/0014/0309211307291pc01b.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.betterphoto.com/uploads/processed/0014/0309211307291pc01b.jpg"/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-01 08:10:33.</i></td>', 'Here is a Valentine''s picture 1 minute before the shot... She is always playing an running everywhere, she never stops!She is always laughing a lot, but not as in picture above, it was the first time I could catch a resting, smooth and calm smile like this one, I took the picture when she turned her face to me, I had about one second to shoot her, the second after she was running and playing again. //www.betterphoto.com/uploads/processed/0014/0309211307291pc01b.jpg ', '2003-10-01 09:04:51.000000', '2003-10-01 09:10:33.000000', 0),
